[{"category":"section","location":"slots/#Slots","page":"Slots","text":"Data structures similar to a Vector.\n\njulia> using LogicalOperators: AND, OR, XOR, NOT, ∧, ∨, ⊕, ¬\n\njulia> AND(1, 2) == 1 ∧ 2\ntrue\n\njulia> OR{Int}(1, 2, 3) == 1 ∨ 2 ∨ 3\ntrue\n\njulia> NOT(true) == ¬true\ntrue\n\nLaTeX short name unicode operator\n\\wedge ∧ AND\n\\vee ∨ OR\n\\oplus ⊕ XOR\n\\neg ¬ NOT","title":"Slots"},{"category":"type","location":"slots/#LogicalOperators.AND","page":"Slots","text":"struct AND{T} <: AbstractSlot{T}\n    elements::Vector{T} where T\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.AND"},{"category":"type","location":"slots/#LogicalOperators.OR","page":"Slots","text":"struct OR{T} <: AbstractSlot{T}\n    elements::Vector{T} where T\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.OR"},{"category":"type","location":"slots/#LogicalOperators.XOR","page":"Slots","text":"struct XOR{T} <: AbstractSlot{T}\n    elements::Vector{T} where T\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.XOR"},{"category":"type","location":"slots/#LogicalOperators.NOT","page":"Slots","text":"struct NOT{T} <: AbstractSlot{T}\n    elements::Vector{T} where T\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.NOT"},{"category":"type","location":"slots/#LogicalOperators.AbstractSlot","page":"Slots","text":"abstract type AbstractSlot{T} end\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.AbstractSlot"},{"category":"macro","location":"slots/#LogicalOperators.@add_slot","page":"Slots","text":"macro add_slot(Op::Symbol)\n\n\n\n\n\nmacro add_slot(ops::Symbol...)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.@add_slot"},{"category":"section","location":"logic/#@logic","page":"@logic","text":"To help understanding the bitwise (&, |), short-circuiting booleans (&&, ||).\n\njulia> using LogicalOperators\n\njulia> @logic 3 & 10\n   0b0011  3\n & 0b1010 10\n   0b0010  2\n2\n\njulia> @logic 10 | 7\n   0b1010 10\n | 0b0111  7\n   0b1111 15\n15\n\njulia> @logic 3 & 10 | 7\n   0b0011  3\n & 0b1010 10\n   0b0010  2\n | 0b0111  7\n   0b0111  7\n7\n\njulia> @logic 3 & (10 | 7)\n   0b1010 10\n | 0b0111  7\n   0b1111 15\n   0b0011  3\n & 0b1111 15\n   0b0011  3\n3\n\nHexagrams 卦 example.\n\njulia> using LogicalOperators\n\njulia> using Hexagrams.八卦\n\njulia> @logic ⊻(乾, 坤)\n   0b111 乾\n ⊻ 0b000 坤\n   0b111 乾\n卦(0x07)\n\njulia> using LogicalOperators\n\njulia> x = 3;\n\njulia> @logic x > 1\nx > 1\ntrue\n\njulia> @logic x < 1 || x > 10 && x isa Int\nx < 1 || x > 10 && x isa Int\nfalse","title":"@logic"},{"category":"macro","location":"logic/#LogicalOperators.@logic","page":"@logic","text":"macro logic(n::Integer)\n\n\n\n\n\nmacro logic(expr::Expr)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LogicalOperators.@logic"},{"category":"section","location":"#LogicalOperators.jl","page":"Home","text":"https://github.com/wookay/LogicalOperators.jl","title":"LogicalOperators.jl 🧩"}]
